 ## Overview
-A renderer for 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) files that supports VR, camera navigation, and optional spherical harmonic (SH) rendering, using either a C++ radix sort or a GPU-based multi-radix sort for depth sorting [S1, unofficial]. It decodes a 3D Gaussian Splat radiance-field cloud from a PLY file and renders it as hardware-instanced, camera-facing quads on-device [S2, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from general-purpose GPU-sorted renderers by offloading the depth-sorting of splats to a background CPU thread at a configurable rate, allowing the GPU shader to focus solely on rasterization and alpha-blending [S1, unofficial]. This approach trades off sorting latency for reduced GPU overhead, making it suitable for mobile XR hardware where computational budgets are shared with other system tasks [S1, unofficial].
+A renderer for 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) files that supports VR, camera navigation, and optional spherical harmonic (SH) rendering, using either a C++ radix sort or a GPU-based multi-radix sort for depth sorting [S1, unofficial]. It decodes a 3D Gaussian Splat radiance-field cloud from a PLY file and renders it as hardware-instanced, camera-facing quads on-device [S2, unofficial]. It supports both desktop and mobile XR environments, with configurable sorting backends (CPU vs GPU) and optional sRGB framebuffer conversion to reduce color banding [S1, unofficial].
 
